c11c8e40fff7b5437d71d0f373d968d6ecdcf62b5da2309c970bbec4af174504","tags":["sailing"],"taken":"2017-04-16 17:53:20","title":"IMG_1864","uploaded":"2017-05-17 14:43:32","width":5419},"33914445673":{"albums":[{"id":"72157643911711523","position":8242}],"bytes":2912326,"camera_position":8242,"comments":[{"author":"50167308@N06","date":"2017-05-18 08:11:28","text":"Looks like the new strategy we just discussed in the office ...\n:-)"},{"author":"100330886@N04","date":"2017-05-18 12:35:05","text":"Haha!  Many materials, like tempered glass, are made stronger by internally opposed forces.  Perhaps offices as well?  \n\nBy the way, the guy in the hat just got back from Germany and wrote about it here: www.tidalpool.org/2017/05/15/mosel.html"},{"author":"100330886@N04","date":"2017-05-18 12:41:47","text":"Looks like he wrote about Berlin too: www.tidalpool.org/2017/05/15/berlin.html"},{"author":"50167308@N06","date":"2017-05-27 03:29:28","text":"Great fun to read a view from someone coming from outside about the Mosel valley and its wines. His statement on sweet wines related to \u201ctaste of the older generation\u201d is very much true. Blame it on the describtion of diabetes related to wine classifications that my coffee ended up in my keyboard \u2026\nIs it your brother? Next I will read through his Berlin blog.\nKind regards (still with tears in my eyes)\nJo"},{"author":"100330886@N04","date":"2017-05-29 17:28:35","text":"Ha!  :)  Honorary brother maybe :)"}],"description":"","detail":"photos/0137.json","filename":"33914445673_1358c9fbe5_o.jpg","flickr_url":"https://www.flickr.com/photos/earthwandering/33914445673/","height":2972,"id":"33914445673","kind":"photo","license":"All Rights Reserved","original":"originals/33914445673/33914445673_1358c9fbe5_o.jpg","sha256":"a25373c9aa849cb177653464df9bf2f711f3e784d980b359ee1cea0f42947827","tags":["sailing"],"taken":"2017-04-15 17:11:53","title":"IMG_1741","uploaded":"2017-05-17 15:20:00","width":4917},"33915501814":{"albums":[